  "question": {
    "text": "In the sulphur estimation, 0.20 g of a pure organic compound gave 0.40 g of barium sulphate. The percentage of sulphur in the compound is ______ $\\times 10^{-1} \\%$.\n(Molar mass : $\\mathrm{O}=16, \\mathrm{~S}=32, \\mathrm{Ba}=137$ in $\\mathrm{g} \\mathrm{mol}^{-1}$ )",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "275",
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{array}{ll}\\text { Organic Compound } \\longrightarrow & \\mathrm{BaSO}_4 \\\\ 0.20 \\mathrm{gm} & 0.40 \\mathrm{gm} \\\\ & \\frac{0.40}{233} \\mathrm{~mol}\\left(\\mathrm{BaSO}_4\\right) \\\\ & \\frac{0.40}{233} \\mathrm{~mol} \\text { (Sulphur) } \\\\ & \\frac{0.40}{233} \\times 32 \\mathrm{gm} \\text { (sulphur) }\\end{array}$\n\n\n\n$\\% \\mathrm{~S}=\\frac{\\frac{0.40 \\times 32}{233} \\times 100}{0.20}=27.5 \\%$ or $275 \\times 10^{-1} \\%$",
    "image": null
  },
